{"key": "6840", "mpkey": "4871", "stat": "A", "schd": "A", "code": "NS 321", "section": "001", "crn": "13289", "title": "EVOLUTION OF WARFARE", "session_html": "Full Term (11 week; Fall/Winter/Spring/Summer) (09-23-2026 to 12-04-2026)", "hours_html": "5", "rpt_for_credit": "", "campus": "Oregon State - Corvallis", "sche_type_clss_fild": "Lecture", "inst_mthd": "In-Person Section", "grade_mode": "Normal Grading Mode", "status": "Open", "max_enroll": "22", "enrollment": "4", "ssbsect_seats_avail": "18", "waitlist_capacity": "0", "ssbsect_wait_count": "0", "ssbsect_wait_avail": "0", "cross_list_max_enroll": "", "xlist_wait_cap": "", "ssbxlst_seats_avail": "", "description": "Examines how warfare philosophies, domains, tactics and technology have either endured or changed. Affirms the fundamental human dimension of warfare, exploring the moral forces at play within warrior cultures. Through the study of history, seeks to illuminate the timeless lessons of warfare. Utilizes case study, lecture, and war gaming in order to set conditions for doctrinal training and professional refinement in subsequent training. Equips students with a strong mental foundation for leading in future conflicts.", "registration_restrictions": "", "corequisites": "", "department_approval_required": "", "recommendations": "Critical thinking, problem-solving, and writing skills", "fees": "", "attribute_description": "", "books_html": "No-cost: Course utilizes open educational resources, materials available through the library, or does not require any purchased materials.", "clssnotes": "<p>Books only provided for registered ROTC students.\n<p><a href=\"http://oregonstate.edu/registrar/rtfiles/q.html?\n:&202701&NS&321&001&13289\" target=\"blank\">Textbooks</a></p>", "meeting_html": "<div class=\"meet\">MWF 10am-11:40am<span class=\"meet-room-202701\"> in <a href=\"https://map.oregonstate.edu/?id=2243#!m/1027688?share\" target=\"_blank\">CASC 137 - Cascade Hall 137</a></span><span class=\"meet-dates